# Multi-Tier Web Application on AWS (VPC, ALB, EC2, RDS)

A PHP "waitlist" signup page (Nova) running on an Apache web server in a custom VPC. Traffic comes in through an Application Load Balancer, and signups are stored in an Amazon RDS MySQL database.

## Architecture

```
Internet
   │
   ▼
Application Load Balancer (HTTP:80)  ──►  Target group (web-sever-tg)
                                                │
                                                ▼
                              EC2 web server (Apache + PHP)  ── public subnet
                                                │  MySQL (3306)
                                                ▼
                              RDS MySQL (teks-database)  ── DB subnet group
```

| Component | Details |
|---|---|
| Region | us-east-1 (N. Virginia) |
| VPC | `my project vpc`, CIDR `10.0.0.0/16`, DNS resolution and hostnames enabled |
| Subnets | public subnet 1 `10.0.1.0/24` (us-east-1a), public subnet 2 `10.0.2.0/24` (us-east-1b), private subnet 1 `10.0.3.0/24` (us-east-1a), private subnet 2 `10.0.4.0/24` (us-east-1b) |
| Routing | `my project igw` attached to the VPC; public route table routes to the IGW; separate private route table for the private subnets |
| Web server | EC2 Ubuntu instance in public subnet 1, running Apache and PHP |
| Database | RDS MySQL `teks-database` (db.t3.micro), subnet group `myproject-db-subnet-grp`, security group `RDS-SG`, port 3306 |
| Load balancer | ALB `web-sever-abl`, listener HTTP:80 forwarding to target group `web-sever-tg` (target type: instance) |

