### 4. Database setup
From the web server, connected to RDS with the `mysql` client, created the `waitlist` database and table, and inserted test rows.

![Tables and insert](images/11-mysql-tables-and-insert.png)
![Table structure](images/12-mysql-describe-waitlist.png)

Table schema:

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| id | int | primary key, auto increment |
| firstname | varchar(100) | not null |
| email | varchar(150) | not null |
| created_at | timestamp | defaults to current time |

### 5. Load balancer (ALB)
Created an Application Load Balancer with an HTTP:80 listener that forwards to a target group, then registered the EC2 instance as a target.

![Listener](images/13-alb-listener.png)
![Listener default action](images/14-alb-listener-forward-to-target-group.png)
![Target group](images/15-target-group.png)

### 6. Result
The Nova waitlist page is served through the ALB DNS name, and new signups appear in the database and in the "Recent Signups" list.

