## Key takeaways

- Designing a VPC with public and private subnets across two AZs.
- Connecting an app server to a managed database inside a VPC with security groups.
- Putting an ALB and target group in front of an EC2 web server.
- Reading Apache and MySQL errors to find the real cause.

## Possible improvements

- Make the database not publicly accessible and allow port 3306 only from the web server's security group.
- Run web servers in an Auto Scaling group across both AZs.
- Move DB credentials to AWS Secrets Manager and add HTTPS with an ACM certificate.
- Rebuild the whole stack with Terraform.
